      "title": "Rated flow at rated pressure — guaranteed",
      "description": "Fire pumps are certified to deliver rated flow at rated pressure, at least 150 % of rated flow at not less than 65 % of rated pressure, with churn (shut-off) pressure not above 140 % of rated (NFPA 20 style rules — verify against the governing edition). The diesel driver gives independence from the electrical supply; it starts automatically on a pressure drop, has two battery sets, and is tested weekly. The jockey pump makes up small leaks so the main pump starts only for a real demand.",
